---
description: Ban browser-default selects and other user-agent form chrome in Helios UI
alwaysApply: true
---

# No native form chrome

Never ship **user-agent** (browser-default) form controls in Helios UI. That includes unstyled or system-looking `<select>` dropdowns, default search boxes, and invisible overlay `<select>` hacks (`opacity: 0` + `position: absolute; inset: 0`). Those open a native picker (often a bar at the top of the page) and break Helios visual language.

Use Helios controls instead:

- Closed option lists: `HeliosMenu` (`app/components/helios-menu.tsx`) or the Analytics `analytics-filter` button + menu (not a raw `<select>`)
- Exclusive choices: `.segmented` / `.segmented__item`
- Text: `.helios-field-input` or existing Hub field classes

```tsx
// BAD — native picker, can overlay the page
<select value={type} onChange={(e) => setType(e.target.value)}>
  <option value="web">Web</option>
</select>

// GOOD
<HeliosMenu label="Search type" value={type} options={options} onChange={setType} />
```

Do not reuse `.analytics-filter__select` unless it sits inside a sized `.analytics-filter__shell` with a visible value label. Prefer `HeliosMenu` for new work.
